  "lineage": "Deep funk is a rare-funk-45 DJ and collecting scene, strongly associated with Keb Darge’s London club activity, rather than merely a low-frequency version of funk. The authored band model selects Sharon Jones and the Dap-Kings, whom Darge directly connects to his night: lead vocal, clipped electric guitar, electric bass, drums and a saxophone/trumpet section. It represents contemporary recorded funk within the scene, not every historical single in a DJ set.",
